# Qt 6.11's QThreadPool synchronization lives in the uninstrumented Qt shared
# library. With ignore_noninstrumented_modules enabled, TSan cannot observe the
# enqueue/dequeue happens-before edge and intermittently reports the inline
# QtConcurrent task constructor racing its inline run method. Keep this narrow:
# the PagedTrackModel page generator and every other application frame remain
# instrumented.
race:QtConcurrent::RunFunctionTaskBase<trackknife::qtmodels::PagedTrackModel::Page>::run
# Same uninstrumented-Qt happens-before gap, second inline template instance:
# the future result store for the Trackbench probe queue's ProbeOutcome batch
# is cleared on the UI thread after the worker's emplaceResult, with the real
# synchronization inside the Qt shared library.
race:QtPrivate::ResultStoreBase::clear<std::vector<trackknife::bench::BenchMainWindow::ProbeOutcome*
# Third inline template instance of the same gap: the MPD album-art fetch
# clears its QImage future result store on the UI thread after the worker's
# emplaceResult, synchronized inside the uninstrumented Qt library.
race:QtPrivate::ResultStoreBase::clear<QImage
# Fourth inline template instance of the same gap: the folder tree clears
# its DirectoryListing future result store on the UI thread after the
# worker's emplaceResult, synchronized inside the uninstrumented Qt library.
